// How bodies move over the ground (D32). Placeholder values, tuned by play.
//
// walk_speed_cm_per_s: walking speed on the reference terrain (cost 10),
//                      in centimetres per game second. 143 is a calm walk.
// terrain_costs:       cost of crossing one tile of each terrain, 10 being
//                      the reference; paths weigh tiles by it and bodies
//                      slow down by it (cost 15 = two thirds of the speed).
//                      None cannot be walked. Every terrain must appear.
// carry_capacity_g:    what a body can carry in all, in grams (D35).
//                      20 kg: thirteen branches, or fifty flints.
// speed_percent_at_full_load: walking speed at full load, in percent of
//                      the unloaded speed; linear in between.
// sight_tiles:         how far a body sees, in tiles on each axis, by the
//                      terrain where it stands when it sets off: the most
//                      open walkable tile among its own and the eight
//                      around it, so at a wood's edge it sees out (D32). A
//                      way round (a ford, a bridge, the end of a pond) is
//                      taken only within that square; past it the body
//                      walks straight toward its target, stops at the
//                      first thing in the way and looks again from there,
//                      as long as each look is nearer the target than the
//                      last; then the player finds the way: exploring and
//                      knowing the ways is the game. 60 m in the open,
//                      25 m in the heart of a wood. A body never
//                      stands on water or rock; their values apply only to
//                      a body put there by mistake. Every terrain must
//                      appear.
// path_budget_tiles:   tiles a path search may look at before it gives up
//                      and the body walks straight. 1500 finds the way
//                      round an obstacle up to thirty or forty tiles
//                      across in the open; the search then costs under
//                      half a millisecond however it ends.
// searches_per_tick:   path searches the world runs in one tick at most;
//                      the rest wait for the next tick, in the order they
//                      came. A click waits a tick or two at worst when a
//                      whole tribe sets off at once.
(
    carry_capacity_g: 20000,
    speed_percent_at_full_load: 60,
    walk_speed_cm_per_s: 143,
    sight_tiles: {
        grass: 60,
        forest: 25,
        ford: 60,
        brook: 60,
        water: 60,
        rock: 60,
    },
    path_budget_tiles: 1500,
    searches_per_tick: 40,
    terrain_costs: {
        grass: Some(10),
        forest: Some(15),
        ford: Some(20),
        brook: Some(15),
        water: None,
        rock: None,
    },
)
